.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt VORBIS-EDIT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vorbis-edit
.Nd edit the comments of an Ogg Vorbis file in an editor
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar file.ogg
.Nm
.Fl h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
lists the comments (the tags) of an Ogg Vorbis file into a temporary
file, one
.Ql NAME=value
per line, opens it in an editor, and writes the comments back,
replacing them all, once the editor exits 0 having changed the file.
.Pp
An editor that fails, or a file left as it was, writes nothing:
writing the comments rewrites the whole Ogg file, so an edit abandoned
costs nothing.
Should the write fail, the edited comments are kept, and their file
named, so the edit is not lost.
.Pp
Comments are read and written as UTF-8, with
.Ql \en
escapes, so a comment spanning lines stays on one.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h
Print the usage and exit.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width TMPDIR
.It Ev VISUAL
The editor, a command line such as
.Ql emacs -nw .
.It Ev EDITOR
The editor when
.Ev VISUAL
is unset; without either,
.Xr vi 1 .
.It Ev TMPDIR
Where the temporary file is made, instead of
.Pa /tmp .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
The comments were written, or left alone because nothing changed.
.It 1
The file is missing or cannot be both read and written,
.Xr vorbiscomment 1
is missing, the comments cannot be read or written, or the editor
failed.
.It 2
A usage error.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Fix the title of a track:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ vorbis-edit 01-intro.ogg
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vorbiscomment 1
.Sh CAVEATS
Only Ogg Vorbis is edited; the tags of an Opus file need
.Xr opustags 1 .
